2147 │ Good criteria are specific to the form and the commission: a reported feature needs different standards from a technical memo, a eulogy, or a comic monologue. Bad criteria are the generic ones every rubric already has — "clarity", "grammar", "structure", "engaging" — and you never propose those.
2148 │ 
2149 │ Each criterion must be judgeable from the draft alone by reading it once.`;
2150 │ 
2151 │     const user = `THE PIECE
2152 │ - Format: ${format}
2153 │ - Audience: ${audience}
2154 │ - Goal: ${goal}
2155 │ - Tone: ${tone}
2156 │ - Constraints: ${constraints}
2157 │ - Success signal: ${successSignal}
2158 │ 
2159 │ ALREADY IN THE RUBRIC (do not propose these again, or near-duplicates of them):
2160 │ ${args.existingLabels.map((l) => `- ${l}`).join("\n") || "- (nothing yet)"}
2161 │ ${
2162 │   args.draftText?.trim()
2163 │     ? `\nAN EXCERPT OF THE DRAFT, for a sense of what the writer is actually doing:\n${args.draftText.trim().slice(0, 2500)}\n`
2164 │     : ""
2165 │ }
2166 │ TASK: Propose 3 to 5 criteria specific to this piece. For each, give a short name (2-5 words) and one sentence stating what a strong version looks like.
2167 │ 
2168 │ Respond as JSON, and only JSON, in this exact shape:
2169 │ {"criteria": [{"label": "<2-5 words>", "description": "<one sentence>"}]}`;
